{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED for exact head 9af4e564792d3b7a7bc38682ad1c4f36b8d5e29f and artifact 91271d69.\n\nThe accepted detector, target-relative evidence, non-inference, full-object-ID, bounded warning, completion-precedence, carried-or-abandoned, thread-actions, and empty-plan fold-binding conclusions remain sound. The new fold association is correctly scoped: merge_incorporation=prior, empty retirements/successors/changed paths, approval-to-artifact event-id binding, signer identity, and exact candidate identity; it grants no path or succession authority.\n\nOne R3 blocker remains. The note still reserves the approval ref at target_pre_head before commit-tree, then advances it by CAS. A hard crash after that reservation but before the receipt commit leaves the ref at an ordinary target commit with no receipt metadata. The deferred cleanup does not run after a hard crash. The receipt object is absent or unreachable, git log --all cannot recover it, and retry cannot re-plan because create-with-empty-old-value sees the existing reservation. The crash table's 're-plan from scratch' therefore does not work. The ordering prose also contradicts itself: it lists commit-tree before durable admission preflight, then says preflight occurs before the object is written.\n\nRepair narrowly: run the durable admission preflight first; create the off-target receipt object; remeasure the target and workroom frontier and restart if either invalidates the measured metadata; then CAS-create the approval ref directly from absent to the receipt commit. Do not first reserve it at the ordinary target. A crash before the CAS leaves only an ignorable unreachable object; a crash after it is recoverable from the receipt ref; a competing spender loses the empty-old CAS. State the exact receipt metadata validated on retry. Update the crash table and mutation-sensitive tests to prove these boundaries.\n\nArchitecture: the design affects layer 7 Git/CLI receipt creation and recovery and layer 5 fold commitment closure. It keeps repository reads out of the fold and correctly requires implementation-time architecture/merge-reference updates, but the layer-7 recovery contract is not yet crash-safe as written.\n\nSecurity: authority and exact-head checks remain default-deny, the prior receipt cannot retire or publish paths, and no secret or untrusted-input regression is introduced. The stranded approval reservation is an unresolved availability and single-use recovery failure at the Git/durable boundary, so approval is unsafe.\n\nSimplification: remove the intermediate target-head reservation. One off-target object followed by one absent-to-receipt CAS is both simpler and fully resumable; retaining reserve-then-advance creates the otherwise impossible stranded state.\n\nIndependent gates passed: make docs; git diff --check; exact head equals origin/request/merged-head-reconciliation-note-delivery; one commit on main 860ee61a; sole changed path notes/2026-08-31-merged-head-commitment-reconciliation.md; clean tree. Current citations at main 860ee61a were re-derived, including main.go reservation/defer/preflight/advance/recovery, mergeplan.go receipt-parent validation, and fold.go mergedArtifacts identity checks.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:91271d69d81bee5923a428dbe55bf453cf1e215c","head":"9af4e564792d3b7a7bc38682ad1c4f36b8d5e29f","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2a7f0ccdfabd0a62ef459f0237e882fd5b42a0e8\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:cce3b338dc15f1bed995d6f4b8981876b83704a9","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}